# Part 7 — Write the C# code

## Step 12: `WebForm1.aspx.cs`

Open `WebForm1.aspx.cs`. Replace its contents with:

```
using System;
using System.Data;
using System.Data.SqlClient;
using CrystalDecisions.CrystalReports.Engine;

namespace CR1
{
    public partial class WebForm1 : System.Web.UI.Page
    {
        protected void Page_Load(object sender, EventArgs e)
        {
            if (!IsPostBack)
            {
                DataSet ds = new DataSet();

                string conString =
                    @"Data Source=localhost\SQLEXPRESS;Initial Catalog=StudentDB;Integrated Security=True";

                using (SqlConnection con =
                    new SqlConnection(conString))
                {
                    SqlDataAdapter da = new SqlDataAdapter(
                        "SELECT RTRIM(Name) AS Name, " +
                        "RTRIM(ID) AS ID FROM Stud", con);

                    da.Fill(ds, "Stud");
                }

                ReportDocument cryRpt = new ReportDocument();

                cryRpt.Load(
                    Server.MapPath("~/CrystalReport1.rpt"));

                cryRpt.SetDataSource(ds);

                Session["StudentReport"] = cryRpt;
            }

            if (Session["StudentReport"] != null)
            {
                CrystalReportViewer1.ReportSource =
                    Session["StudentReport"];
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Save the file.

### What this code does

1. Connects to `StudentDB`.
2. Retrieves `Name` and `ID` from `Stud`.
3. Stores the records in a `DataSet`.
4. Loads `CrystalReport1.rpt`.
5. Supplies the dataset to the report.
6. Displays the report using `CrystalReportViewer1`.

The session keeps the report available when the viewer performs postbacks, such as paging through the report.

